-- Newsroom drafts for 2026-11-21 (Saturday). Loaded once into EDITORIAL_REVIEW; an editor approves before anything is published.
-- Facts restated in Boston Daily's own words with attribution. Every story carries its own photo; none was used in an earlier package or open draft (grepped content/, seed/ and the open newsroom/2026-11-19 and newsroom/2026-11-20 branches).
-- loc.gov and Wikimedia Commons could not be opened from the newsroom sandbox on this run. Photo URLs are Wikimedia Commons thumbnails built from file names confirmed by search (MD5 path). The editor should confirm each license on the file page. The image check falls back to 800px or the original file if a thumbnail size is missing.
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO stories (id, slug, lane, type, section_slug, status, sensitive, headline, dek, body, byline, hero_image_url, hero_image_credit, hero_image_rights, source_system, source_ref, priority, is_lead_candidate, created_by, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bd-20261121-trump-asia-news-conference', 'trump-white-house-news-conference-asia-trip-xi-putin-lutnick-cairncross', 'newsroom', 'news_story', 'white-house', 'EDITORIAL_REVIEW', 0, 'Trump calls his Asia trip a historic success at a nearly two-hour White House news conference', 'Back from Shenzhen, the president said on Friday, Nov. 20, that he met more than 20 leaders in four days, stood by Commerce Secretary Howard Lutnick and warned Democrats he would veto their bills unless they work with him.', 'President Trump used a White House news conference on Friday, Nov. 20, to describe his trip to Asia as one of the most successful presidential visits to the region in American history, CBS News reported. The session was scheduled for noon ET, started late and ran nearly two hours.

## The trip

Trump said he met more than 20 world leaders over four days and secured two new trade deals, according to CBS News. He spoke a day after the first sit-down of the leaders of the United States, China and Russia, held in Shenzhen on Thursday, Nov. 19.

The joint "peace declaration" issued after that meeting did not mention Russia''s war in Ukraine or the U.S. war with Iran, PBS NewsHour reported. It called for United Nations reforms, more oil supply and lower nuclear risks, without spelling out what the U.N. changes would be.

Trump also said Russian President Vladimir Putin told him the 2022 invasion of Ukraine would not have happened had Trump been president. CBS News noted that was Trump''s account of a private conversation.

## Cabinet and staff

Asked about a reported rift between Lutnick and Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent over chip sales to China, Trump said he had not lost confidence in Lutnick, CBS News reported. He also said he would like to see Jensen Huang return as Nvidia''s chief executive.

CBS News reported that National Cyber Director Sean Cairncross is leaving the administration; several sources told the network he was fired. Kirsten Davies has been named to replace him, pending Senate confirmation.

## Congress

With Democrats set to control the House in January, Trump said he would veto Democratic-led legislation unless Democrats work with him, and he called Democratic Leader Hakeem Jeffries "a smart guy," according to CBS News. Vice President JD Vance praised the Senate-passed permitting bill, saying it would pay dividends.', 'Boston Daily Staff', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/East_Room_of_the_White_House,_Washington,_D.C._LCCN2002695413.jpg/1280px-East_Room_of_the_White_House,_Washington,_D.C._LCCN2002695413.jpg', 'East Room of the White House (historic file photo). Library of Congress via Wikimedia Commons (editor to confirm the "no known restrictions" rights statement on the file page)', 'public_domain', 'newsroom', 'content/2026-11-21.sql', 9, 1, 'newsroom-assistant', '2026-11-21T11:00:00.000Z', '2026-11-21T11:00:00.000Z');
